The attached image, Figure 2, demonstrates the in vivo kinetics of Nano-11, showing its retention at the injection site and subsequent clearance over time without systemic distribution. Panel A illustrates the fluorescent signal of labeled Nano-11 remaining localized at the calf muscle injection site over 21 days. Panel B confirms the absence of Nano-11 in internal organs after 21 days. Panel C quantifies the injection site fluorescence intensity, revealing an initial decrease, a temporary increase by day 2 (attributed to edema), and a steady decline, with approximately 20% of the original signal remaining after 21 days.